  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Breakaway – through ball with a chaser on your back",
  "description": "A goal with a goalkeeper and two cones a little way out from goal, a few metres apart. The passer B stands with balls on the other side of the centre line. The attacker A and the chaser X start in front of goal. Work in groups of three while the rest wait.\n\nA runs out towards the cones with X following and checks over the shoulder twice to find B. B plays the ball between the cones to A, who receives, rounds the nearest cone and attacks the goal. X rounds the other cone and backchecks to catch up before the shot. Rotation: A becomes the chaser, B the attacker and X the passer.\n\nVariant: the chaser does not have to round the cone, so the attacker has less time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Check over your shoulder before the ball arrives – know where the passer and the chaser are."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "First touch forwards, away from the chaser."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Full speed at goal and shoot before the chaser catches up."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Chaser: run back towards the slot, not towards the ball."
    }
  ],
